# Built-in end-to-end scenario (phone-shell --selftest). Every step runs the
# real stack: shell <-> app processes (phone.Ui) <-> broker <-> mediad/keystored.
# "#part <name>" lines split it for go test ./shell (TestSelftestScenario),
# phone-shell --parallel (make selftest, make pixel-selftest, make cts) and
# the emulators: each part runs on a stack of its own, from a new boot's
# idle screen, in parallel with the others. A case belongs to the part named
# above it: one that needs what an earlier case left (a paired headset, a
# call in the log, a photo) goes in that case's part. A part's snapshots
# are compared with the same baselines whether it runs alone or after the
# others in one Shell, so what a case leaves that another part could see
# (notifications, pairings, apps, files) goes again at its end.

# The boot animation plays first.
sleep 800
snap 00-boot

#part chat
